{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfBSJouLRSxDbmSRdCkgN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I submitted index 3 (Ca 0.50, Mn 0.50) as the best composition. It gave the highest photocurrent of the three samples I measured, though with only three points I can't be sure it's the true best in the library.\n\n| Index | Ca : Mn | Photocurrent |\n|---|---|---|\n| 16 | 0.14 : 0.86 (manganese-rich) | 4e-8 A |\n| **3** | **0.50 : 0.50** | **1.7e-7 A** |\n| 24 | 0.65 : 0.35 (calcium-rich) | 2e-8 A |\n\n- **How I spent the budget:** the library had 27 compositions but only 3 merit measurements. I measured the 1:1 composition and one sample from each end of the line, then ranked them.\n- **What the data suggests:** photocurrent rises from the manganese-rich end to the middle and falls sharply on the calcium-rich side. The 1:1 ratio matches the known CaMnO₃ phase, which may be why that sample does best. I didn't confirm that phase, though: I used none of the 5 XRD measurements.\n- **Main gap:** several unmeasured compositions sit close to 1:1, for example index 6 (Ca 0.53), index 18 (Ca 0.47) and index 12 (Ca 0.43). Any of them could beat index 3, and the budget ran out before I could check."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":367,"cache_read_input_tokens":7969,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":367},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6772759f-90f1-4da3-9d0f-5eb5148acc87","uuid":"08715dfa-efa6-48be-b218-5a0032a904c7","timestamp":"2026-09-18T19:13:20.014Z","request_id":"req_011CfBSJoAfyGkeTG9i7cTzv"}
